  "text": "A delivery manager walked into Monday's release meeting already knowing what needed to happen: engineering was going to stop building new features for the week and fix defects instead. She didn't open with that. She thanked the team for the work they'd already done. She walked through the previous sprint, acknowledged the pressure everyone already felt around the release, and explained the stakeholder feedback and the defects testing had turned up. She wanted people to have context before she asked them to change direction, and she didn't want the release to sound worse than it already was.",
